From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: koalabuttz <27229333+koalabuttz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 05:23:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] refactor: name the DvarFlags bits above 0x80 by what the code
 does

DVAR_AUTOEXEC and DVAR_CHANGEABLE_RESET sat on each other's bits:
Dvar_SetCommand adds 0x8000 while an autoexec config loads, and
Dvar_ChangeResetValue asserts on 0x200. DVAR_TEMP (0x100) is the bit
the server sends as the CS_CODINFO configstrings, so it becomes
DVAR_CODINFO. DVAR_NORESTART (0x400) is the serverinfo bit that script
setDvar adds and Dvar_ResetScriptInfo clears on map load, so it becomes
DVAR_SCRIPTINFO.

Rename only: every use keeps its numeric value. The literals 256, 1024,
0x404, 0x9200 and 0x8000 at those sites now use the names. This answers
the naming question in upstream issue 30.
